^["survey"]{
 as_of: "2026-10-13, a read-only survey at 76e17bd4, spot-checked"
 size: "packages/spw-runtime/src: 36 files, 6,696 lines; register-bank.ts 899 lines is the only file past 600; hot-session.ts has 17 import statements"
 mixes: [
  "register-bank: value algebra, memory budget and eviction, get and set, phase and lens, liminality, marks, coupling, provenance",
  "hot-session: cache keys, evaluate, inspect, interconnect, a cite and follow pointer store, invalidation",
  "stages: precipitate types, the runSpwStepped generator, .spw rendering",
  "interpreter: one evaluate switch of 19 cases over about 200 lines"
 ]
 legacy: "88 of 89 non-test files under src/seed and src/runtime are one-line re-exports; their consumers are legacy tests, which tsconfig.typecheck.json never checks; 4 of the runtime suite's files test the CLI"
 hashes: "sha256 cut to 16 hex is copied four times (runtime hot-session-types, path-receipt, sense-cycle; seed patch); FNV readers hash UTF-16 units; range-transform contentHash slices an 8-char hash to 16"
 portability: "runtime and seed import no outer package and have no relative cycles; the seed index reaches node:crypto (nest-path, stencil, patch) and Buffer (self-mass), the parser and reader entries do not; the runtime root re-exports node-only site-install and composition-eval"
 health: "test:runtime 190 of 190; test:seed 853 of 853; tsc clean"
 duplicates: "nowIso, isRuntimeRecord, and clamp01 have several copies; runtimeMagnitude and valueMagnitude measure differently; runtime OPERATOR_AFFINITIES names ., $, and <> differently from the LSP sigil table"
}

^["risk_model"]{
 hard_failures: ["a persisted hash or cache key changes without a receipt", "a split changes the public RegisterBank or HotSession surface a mounted consumer uses"]
 soft_failures: ["moved tests lose a fixture path", "a dead-export prune removes something a consumer imports"]
 non_negotiables: ["test:runtime, test:seed, and tsc stay green at every commit", "the parser and reader bundles never reach a node built-in"]
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-10-13 21:30] observe — A read-only survey of the runtime and seed found one file past the size guard (register-bank, 899 lines), one past the import guard (hot-session, 17), 88 one-line shims kept alive only by legacy tests that are never type-checked, four copies of a sha256-to-16 helper beside FNV hashes of UTF-16 units, and a contentHash that slices 8 characters to 16. No layering violations or relative cycles. Details in the survey frame.
 >>[2026-10-13 21:30] decide — The owner asked for runtime refactoring and maintenance planning. This plan holds the moves no plan owned; the stages split goes to precipitate-model-alignment, the package DAG check stays with refactor-import-sprawl, and sigil-table convergence with audit-ui-data-models.
 >>[2026-10-13 22:04] note — Branches waiting to merge on 2026-10-13: feature/reader-bundle adds seed's browser-safe reader entry, which node_free_seed_root extends to the whole seed index.
 >>[2026-10-13 22:33] note — From the module-trees survey: land split_hot_session as session/hot/ (the four hot-session files plus the pointer store), so the 18-file session/ reads as two concerns; site-install.ts holds mount resolution, which runtime_node_subpath should name.
 >>[2026-10-13 22:57] implement — Landed on feature/browser-workbench: node_free_seed_root (0bf89a77) and runtime_node_subpath (900e2b9c). Seed and the runtime hash with canonical/content-hash.ts sha256Hex, a synchronous SHA-256 over UTF-8 bytes whose digests equal node:crypto's, so no stored hash moved and ?[persisted_hashes] is not yet forced. one_hash_module now has its home in content-hash.ts; the FNV hashes over UTF-16 units still wait for it.
 >>[2026-10-13 23:16] implement — Landed on feature/reader-form-context: one_hash_module (eb34e6c3) gives seed textHash, 16 hex of SHA-256 over UTF-8 bytes; hashString, geometry cards, and transform preconditions use it, the two FNV hashes are gone, and range-transform's no-op slice ends; the runtime spells its three hashes as textHash (7509cbb8). SHA-256 costs 110 ms over the 9.5 MB corpus against 53 ms for FNV. Resolved ?[persisted_hashes].
 >>[2026-10-19 16:28] revise — Direction review at 0eb1d1c0: portability and unified hashes have landed; mark active, prioritize test ownership, and gate splits on behavioral evidence.
 >>[2026-10-27 10:18] note — docs/runtime/md/runtime-memory.md documents the RegisterBank memory-budget surface (setMemoryBudget, memoryPressure, enforceMemoryBudget, purgeColdCells, setFacetEvictable) and the keys eviction never drops; split_register_bank must keep that surface, so the doc is now a root. Declared shares with typescript-perf-audit-infra over tsconfig.typecheck.json: legacy_tests_home widens what that config checks, which moves the baseline its perf rows measure. Checked against main at 850077ab: nothing past runtime_node_subpath has landed; register-bank.ts is still 899 lines and hot-session.ts still has 17 imports.
 >>[2026-10-27 10:26] note — From the 2026-10-27 sweep (precipitate-model-alignment test_precipitate_order): the runtime stage-order test sits inside if (result.success), so a failed run passes it. When legacy_tests_home moves normalize.test.ts, dropping that guard costs nothing and makes the test able to fail.
 >>[2026-11-06 18:10] observe — A mounted consumer that compiles the packages from source under its own tsconfig (a Vite app aliasing spw-workbench/runtime to packages/spw-runtime/src/index.ts) could not move from fffab72 to main: site-install.ts imports node:fs and node:path and is reachable from the runtime index, so the root does not run in a browser; canonical/snippet.ts assigns readonly tuples to string[] (TS4104) under the consumer's compiler settings though this repo's build passes; and RegisterId is now branded, so a consumer passing plain strings breaks at about ten sites. The consumer took the reader build instead for its slot reader and kept fffab72 for the runtime. Evidence for the browser-root slice: a runtime index with no node built-in reachable, and a published type surface consumers compile against instead of this repo's sources.
 >>[2026-11-06 20:20] note — parser-releases typed_variants is the other way out for the source-compiling consumer recorded above: with types shipped beside workbench.min.js, which already exports all five runtime values the consumer imports, it can drop the March copy without this repo making every source file compile under its settings.
 >>[2026-11-09 17:44] implement — legacy_tests_home is prepared in the working tree at main@edbc5500, uncommitted. 56 files moved with git mv beside the sources they exercise: 12 runtime tests and their fixtures to packages/spw-runtime, 4 CLI tests to packages/spw-cli, 29 seed tests and the golden snapshots to packages/spw-seed, 3 analyzer tests beside their scripts. Two files are new: pipeline/stages.test.ts holds the ten stage tests cut from normalize.test.ts, and one loadConfig test went to packages/spw-lsp because a runtime test cannot import the language server. Collection parity over eight suites: 2,039 test names before, 2,048 after, none vanished, and the nine added are the trial bench. tsconfig.typecheck.json no longer excludes any test, and tsc is clean. Seven test files needed type fixes (branded register keys, ast narrowing), with no any and no changed assertion beyond the stage guard, which now asserts success. run-spw.test.ts inlines the two harness calls it used, since a package test importing src/testing broke the package build.
 >>[2026-11-09 17:44] implement — retire_src_shims is prepared in the same tree, uncommitted: 87 of 88 shims deleted, each checked first as a one-line mirror of its package twin. The premise that only legacy tests used the shims was false in one place: a mounted consumer build aliases src/runtime/index.ts through its own pinned mount, so that file stays with a README naming why. src/seed/docs holds four real files (637 lines) and stays; its index still lists the retired layout. 15 .spw refs in four files that resolved into shim directories now point at the packages, and the runtime filename check walks packages/spw-runtime/src. Baseline failures are unchanged and not from this work: three in scripts/analyzers/__tests__ and one in the language server form-context test. Follow-ups are named in commits: the compatibility index, the seed docs home, 133 prose mentions, the analyzer test twins, the layer check target, and the dead wonder-axioms test.
 >>[2026-11-09 17:50] implement — legacy_tests_home landed as 891e93b9 and retire_src_shims as 1a1b95bb, on feature/runtime-maintenance, authorized by the owner. Next is the value algebra.
 >>[2026-11-11 23:54] implement — runtime_value_module, uncommitted on main: state/runtime-value.ts holds the record, frame and packet guards, the deep copy, the merge, the uncapped magnitude and nowIso, and register-bank imports them (899 to 818 lines). Two behaviours changed, each with a test: a packet is told by its closed kind set, so a plain record with a kind field (kind: note) is copied whole with only its own keys instead of gaining payload and tags and sharing its nested values; and a record merge copies the left side too, so the result shares nothing with either. The two magnitudes are named for their difference rather than reconciled: the bank's is uncapped and reads through frames and packets for measure, memory-policy's caps and scales down for residency cost. The interpreter keeps its own looser record guard (any non-array object), which this slice did not touch.
 >>[2026-11-12 00:11] observe — Correction to the 23:54 entry: the two magnitudes were documented for their difference in runtime-value.ts, not renamed. The packet guard also changes access, record merge and magnitude for a record that carries a kind outside the six packet kinds; no runtime source builds a packet with another kind. No feature/runtime-maintenance branch exists, so the slice sits on main beside the earlier ones.
}

