^["done"]{
 # Local history: written incrementally, finalized at merge.
 ~#resolved(persisted_hashes): "When one hash function replaces the copies, do cache keys and session handles drop once and rebuild, while anything a person authored keeps its old hash with a receipt naming the new one? — moot in practice: no tracked file stores an FNV digest (searched 2026-10-13), so the changed values live only in memory and in the ignored .spw/gen/session cache, which rebuilds as the recommended default said; the sha256 callers kept identical digests"
}
